 "title": "Add iSerial field to Native USB devices",
 "user": {
  "login": "facchinm",
  "id": 8843437,
  "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDM0Mzc=",
  "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8843437?v=4",
  "gravatar_id": "",
  "url": "https://api.github.com/users/facchinm",
  "html_url": "https://github.com/facchinm",
  "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/facchinm/followers",
  "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/facchinm/following{/other_user}",
  "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/facchinm/gists{/gist_id}",
  "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/facchinm/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
  "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/facchinm/subscriptions",
  "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/facchinm/orgs",
  "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/facchinm/repos",
  "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/facchinm/events{/privacy}",
  "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/facchinm/received_events",
  "type": "User",
  "user_view_type": "public",
  "site_admin": false
 },
 "body": "Windows PCs always believe that an USB device with a particular triplet of VID/PID/SerialNumber will never change during its existence, thus saving the device's \"nature\" on the Registry. \nWith the introduction of PluggableUSB, a device can change its \"composition\" between a sketch and another if we include different headers. But the new device does not necessarily implement all the capabilities of the one that has been saved, leading to drivers not loading etc.\n\nTo solve this problem, two different approaches where tested:\n- creating a S/N based on the descriptor length (collisions still possible, less overhead)\n- craft a S/N string from the pluggable modules properties (no collision, no difference between different HID submodules) (this seems better)\n\nA call has been added (`getShortName`) and it MUST be implemented by any library based on PluggableUSB. No effect on PluggableHID-based libraries.\n\nThe patchset is composed by two patches (which will be squashed afterwards) to show the first approach on AVR (first patch)\n\n@NicoHood  @matthijskooijman @PaulStoffregen @cmaglie \n",
